[E0418] Error: a `&var` projection cannot lend `LOW`, a constant
   ╭─[ err/228_lending_tables/main.wip:7:34 ]
   │
 7 │ fn writable(): &var [i64] = lend LOW
   │                                  ─┬─
   │                                   ╰─── a constant cannot change
   │
   │ Help: declare the result `&`: a constant is lent for reading
   │
   │ Note: a top-level `val` is kept once, in memory nothing writes
───╯
[E0418] Error: a projection lends a place, and this is a value
   ╭─[ err/228_lending_tables/main.wip:9:25 ]
   │
 9 │ fn limit(): &i64 = lend LIMIT
   │                         ──┬──
   │                           ╰──── a value, not a place
   │
   │ Help: answer it by value: declare the result without `&`
   │
   │ Note: a number, a `bool` or a variant of nothing is written where it is used, even from a top-level `val`, so there is no place to lend
───╯
